cookbook/workflows/profile-cuda-bottlenecks-with-nsight-systems.md:19:Choose non-terminating capture behavior (`--kill=none`, and `--wait=all` where supported) while preserving runner checkpoint/watchdog handling. Never kill or restart a learner merely to satisfy profiling; plan launch-time instrumentation at an authorized safe boundary. CPU sampling permission failures do not by themselves establish CUDA tracing failure. Preserve concrete errors and label fallback evidence; utilization snapshots, VRAM percentages and unsynchronized Python timers cannot establish a kernel bottleneck.
