cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:3:title: "BC bootstrap uses native replay features and current heads"
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:4:description: "Localize zero-bank self-play, prepare exact admitted public actions through Rust, and qualify a separate current-model BC warm start."
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:11:# BC bootstrap uses native replay features and current heads
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:15:The current policy and initial incumbent both end at zero banks in8 native games/seeds7000–7007,16 seat trajectories each. Current-policy mean bank falls from3000 to595.125 after one turn,26.5625 after eight, and zero by192; the initial policy shows the same failure pattern. Removing market orders while retaining model unit commands preserves3000 for every seat through719 turns, as does full PASS. This localizes the observed cash depletion to market behavior rather than a zeroed bank metric. It does not establish an optimal no-trade policy or full engine correctness. Diagnostic action sampling is eager BF16, not a compiled-path numerical parity or speed test.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:17:Both-zero terminal W/L/D gives no ranking signal between these policies. Econ.2 is a capped death-potential difference, not a penalty for arbitrary spending or a bank-profit target. The current-policy diagnostic also accumulates8193 ineffective unit commands; economic production chains remain unlearned. Prior cookbook search found no qualified v3 BC implementation; v2's public replay loader provides observation/action alignment and shared-field semantics, not its model, collector or training code.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:23:- `ops/bc-bootstrap-2026-09-29/select_replays.py`, `prepare.py`: read-only source volume4llk4uaf20, source days09-21..27, seeded32 training and4 validation episodes/day.252 episodes are split by identity, with duplicate episode basenames rejected in preparation. Hash each source payload and prepared shard. Pair observation[t] with action[t+1], fill seat1 schema-shared fields, and preserve own-private encoding. Omitted units are filled with Python `None`, which `actor_codec._unit_frame` rejects; the earlier claim that they become explicit NONE was incorrect. Never truncate market orders or quantities. Replay JSON is processed once offline; resident GPU arrays feed BC minibatches. The [[rebuild-data-preparation-preserves-replay-identity|rebuild Reference]] records the source check and v4 admission consequence; this correction does not alter the historical manifest counts.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:24:- `train_bc.py`: current8,353,727-parameter stateless v3 actor; no v2 weights/model or opponent identity. Reuse current evaluate_actions, compiler, BF16, distributed context and optimizer factory. Mean turn NLL is normalized by active frame count; frozen critic head receives no supervised value target, but shared-trunk updates still change its predictions. Two ranks use64 game rows/128 seat observations per microbatch, accumulation2 and512-seat global optimizer batch. Fresh AdamW state, learning rate1e-4, weight decay.01. This is offline BC, not a second PPO trainer. Validation uses a fixed random subset of held-out episode rows and selects best NLL; it is neither final playing strength nor a promotion.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:25:- `evaluate_bc.py`, `run.sh`, `disable-automatic-ppo`: the75-minute BC run is independent. The owner corrected the earlier automatic-PPO interpretation. The launcher now ends after BC; a remotely verified exit2 guard prevents the already-running wrapper from entering its buffered PPO path. This intentional handoff exit is separate from the BC trainer exit code. Launch manifests remain frozen; changed file hashes and verification are in `handoff-cancellation.json`.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:29:The252-episode slice admits158,772 paired turns (139,835 training;18,937 validation) and rejects22,416/181,188 turns (12.37%). Rejection counts:unknown market command14,007; unsupported unit arguments5621; market-item mask1668; extra hand commands1102; queue limit17; quantity range1. A12-episode inspection identifies `INVALID` market markers among rejected commands. Rejections can bias phase/action coverage; no claim that this slice represents all v2 BC data. Both seats are used without outcome filtering; episode split alone does not prove opponent-general holdout.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:31:Eager two-rank smoke passes8 updates/4096 seat turns with validation NLL3.648→3.575 on two episodes. Full-data compiled two-rank smoke passes8 updates/4096 seat turns with NLL3.925→3.853. Independent checks confirm finite updated actor weights, unchanged critic-head tensors and canonical checkpoint key compatibility. Cold smoke throughput is not a sustained BC benchmark. The original smoke checkpoint metadata included BC-only keys; the harness was corrected and rerun before launch so weights-only handoff uses the canonical schema, with BC metadata in separate artifacts.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:33:BC quality remains unqualified: the fixed held-out subset NLL reaches0.761 at14,600 updates, then degrades to1.954 at75,600 while training loss falls. This is overfitting on the selected corpus; longer runtime alone does not establish improvement. Best weights are retained. Full held-out evaluation, action-level fidelity and free-running economic behavior remain unverified. The owner subsequently requests a separate half-hour PPO from BC best; BC is stopped early for that switch, so there is no completed75-minute BC result. The separate launch is documented in `ops/ppo-from-bc-2026-09-29/plan.md`. It failed: after 3 iterations and only 6 optimizer steps (KL 1.8894/1.0453/0.3651; win rates 12.5/10.55/3.52% against the BC incumbent), rollout hit a CUDA illegal memory access and rank 1 then hit the 600 s NCCL timeout. A later blocking reproduction traced it to a compiler-generated GEMM overflow on the 8,192-row rollout forward, which also corrupted rollout activations. The KL spikes and falling win rates are therefore not evidence against the BC policy ([[compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows|compiler overflow Reference]]). No final checkpoint exists; the BC best and its pre-PPO copy have matching SHA-256. Automatic handoff remains disabled. The planned Isaiah alignment changes the architecture (per-player critic value tokens, possibly model size), so it schedules one BC rerun (`ops/gap-closure-2026-09-29/plan.md`, Phase 4). Preserve the [[../decisions/preserve-the-ppo-recipe-across-bc-bootstrap|PPO recipe]]; do not infer readiness or promotion from these local-loss smoke checks.
