cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:22:- W&B reports a crashed run as finished, a behavior inherited from upstream.
cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:52:Evaluation runs on rank 0 while the other ranks wait for the broadcast, with no per-turn progress log. An idle or collective-waiting GPU during evaluation is not a hang. A 4,096-game evaluation did exceed the 600 s NCCL broadcast timeout; optional `rl.eval_n_games` now sets the evaluation count independently (unset keeps upstream behavior). A smaller count changes selection variance.
cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:60:These measure earlier models or the historical 4096/spm 1/accumulation 2 recipe. They do not qualify the aligned recipe or dense BC positions.
cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:68:Reuse the starter's PPO machinery, DDP, scheduling, optimizer grouping and telemetry without hard-coding Orbit entity/action field names at transport boundaries. Evaluate the two-seat game with its own reward/termination definitions. Preserve behavior action densities from collection through update; changing the action representation must not silently turn joint probabilities into per-slot clipping.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:61:- `tests/kaggriculture/helpers.py`: the heads tests' tiny models, programs and replay cases, moved unchanged in behavior (65 heads tests pass before and after).
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:85:The estimator is Isaiah's: teacher-forced conditionals at the behavior policy's replayed prefix, summed per slot, not an unbiased joint-program KL. Both sides must share the grammar tables and `hire_limit`; replay admission does not detect a mismatch that still admits the program.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/1.3/independent-7b5eacd/review.md:48:The docs/cookbook otherwise accurately describe the R1 v2 policy correction, fixed quotas, 512/1,024 corpus denominators, exact caller-buffer interface, and timing limitation. No optimized timing or reference regeneration was rerun here. The brief explicitly allows the existing optimized-build memory-stop/pod handoff, so that timing gap alone is not a new rejection reason. Pinned/GPU behavior remains unqualified locally.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:3:title: "Kaggriculture BC trainer warm-starts PPO from the held-out best"
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:4:description: "Task 5.2 trainer script: scripts/train_bc.py trains the registered KaggricultureTransformer on teacher-forced replay NLL plus a winner cross-entropy critic target from raw final banks, through Isaiah's factory, optimizer, BF16 autocast, cuBLAS-only compile and DDP seams. It reads the refreshed 5.1 kaggriculture-bc-shard-v1 format into rank-partitioned host memory, keeps every strict held-out-NLL minimum as the best checkpoint in run_ppo's exact schema, stops after sustained non-improvement beyond min_delta (L9), and records each resume as a new attempt with its own source under an unchanged trajectory config. CPU-tested with synthetic shards; no GPU, DDP, compile, real-data or W&B execution yet."
