cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:11:# Kaggriculture BC trainer warm-starts PPO from the held-out best
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:13:Plan Task 5.2 asks for a BC trainer on the rebuilt model that reuses Isaiah's optimizer factory, BF16 and compile path, keeps the best checkpoint by held-out NLL and stops on sustained held-out degradation (lesson L9). This change builds the trainer script and its tests. The BC run itself waits for the Task 5.1 shards and the pod.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:17:- `scripts/train_bc.py`: CLI in `run_ppo.py`'s shape (fresh `CONFIG --data --output-dir`, restart from a run directory, `torchrun` for several GPUs, `--log-mode`, `--wandb-mode online|offline`, `--max-runtime-hours`, `--source-commit` on a fresh launch or a restart). Each launch or restart appends an attempt record to `bc_attempts.jsonl` (see "Restart identity" below). It runs the GEMM workload check for the BC microbatch and validation forwards and the compile-stack check. It then builds the model with `create_model` and `reset_parameters`, compiles through `configure_model_compile` (the Kaggriculture cuBLAS-only claim), builds the optimizer with `create_optimizer` / `create_lr_scheduler` and wraps it with Isaiah's DDP adapter.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:18:- `python/owl/train/bc.py`: `BCConfig`, the objective, `TrainSharding`, `HeldOutSelection`, checkpoint and resume state, a W&B logger (project `kg-v3`, `job_type` `bc`) and `train_bc`. BF16 comes from the PPO config's `rl.dtype` through `autocast_context`. The model, dtype and compile settings come from the PPO config that BC warm-starts (`ppo_config`), so the BC checkpoint matches that PPO run's model. `wrap_bc_model_for_distributed` casts the model for Isaiah's Orbit-annotated DDP adapter, whose dispatch passes Kaggriculture batches through unchanged. The Task 3.1 trainer seam has not generalized those annotations yet.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:19:- `python/owl/kaggriculture/bc_data.py`: the shard writer and loader. `configs/bc/kaggriculture_2rank.yaml`: the 2-rank BC config for `configs/kaggriculture_2rank.yaml`. It sits under `configs/bc/` because the existing config tests load every top-level `configs/*.yaml` as a PPO `FullConfig`. `README.md` has a new "Kaggriculture BC warm start" section.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:23:- **The critic is trained, not frozen.** Isaiah trains all of the shared trunk and both heads together, and his teacher distillation weights policy KL and winner CE equally (`teacher_kl_coef = teacher_value_coef`). BC is distillation from the recorded player. So the loss is the turn NLL divided by program length, plus `value_coef` (1.0) times the per-seat winner CE against the episode's raw final banks (L1: the larger bank wins, a draw is 0.5 each). The reference froze the critic head, but its trunk still moved, so its critic reached PPO miscalibrated with no target. A test shows that a policy-only loss leaves the four `critic_head` tensors without gradients. Isaiah's adapter builds DDP without unused-parameter detection for this model, so the joint loss also gives every parameter a gradient. DDP itself was not run. Isaiah's own recipe used no imitation learning (`docs/write-up.md`); BC here is the plan's owner-required addition.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:26:- **Selection and stopping.** Each evaluation's held-out NLL feeds `HeldOutSelection`, which keeps selection and patience apart. Every strict new minimum is written as `checkpoint_bc_best.pt`, with a SHA-256 record in `checkpoint_bc_best.json`. Patience counts evaluations since the last improvement of more than `min_delta` over the previous such improvement, so gains inside `min_delta` still replace the best checkpoint but do not reset the count (the early-stopping convention; the first version gated the checkpoint by `min_delta` too, which Codex verification r1 showed could discard the lowest NLL). Training stops when that count reaches `patience_evals`, at `max_steps` or at the runtime cap.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:27:- **Restart identity.** A restart is a new attempt, not a continuation of the launch's identity. `bc_attempts.jsonl` gets one record per launch or restart: attempt index, that checkout's source (`git rev-parse HEAD` with a `-dirty` suffix, or `--source-commit`), the lineage of every attempt's source, start step, the parent `bc_state.pt` SHA-256, dataset root and manifest hash, world size and start time. The best-checkpoint record and `bc_result.json` copy the attempt that wrote them. `bc_state.pt` stores the trajectory settings (the BC config except `max_steps`, and the whole PPO config by content); a restart with any other difference fails and names the changed fields, so only the step budget can grow. A changed source is recorded, not rejected: exact replay is claimed only for an unchanged source. `bc_history.jsonl` holds the NLL curve and `bc_result.json` the stopping step and reason. The best checkpoint has exactly `run_ppo.py`'s keys with `env_steps` 0, next to the PPO `config.yaml`.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:40:  - the 2-rank BC config targeting the 2-rank PPO config;
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:42:- Mutation checks (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/5.2/mutations.log`) killed 11 of 12 mutants. The survivor shares one permutation seed across ranks. The rank partitions are disjoint, so it changes no row set. Codex's independent verification r1 (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-5.2-trainer-r1.md`, REJECT) ran 100 mutants (27 killed) and raised the two P2 findings fixed above. Its reported gaps for reversed loss signs and a removed real `optimizer.step()` are now killed by the r1 tests; 11 targeted mutants of the fixes, loss sign, length normalization and the real optimizer step were all killed (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/5.2-r1/mutations.log`). The seven new or changed tests failed before the fix (`5.2-r1/test-bc-red.log`).
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:43:- `just py-prepare` after the r1 fixes: 1,698 passed, 11 skipped, docs-fresh clean (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/5.2-r1/py-prepare.log`).
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:49:- The BC run needs the 5.1 shards. Their token half waits on the Task 1.4 `kaggriculture_encode/decode` binding, and the full-slice run needs a machine that can read volume `4llk4uaf20`. It also needs the pod and FlashAttention, because `configs/model/kaggriculture.yaml` forces it (plan 6.0). PPO from the BC best then needs `run_ppo.py` to run Kaggriculture (Tasks 1.4/3.1). Today only its loaders are exercised.
